You can automate the SAP GUI export to Excel (Spreadsheet → XLSX) using an Excel VBA macro with SAP GUI Scripting. The macro will:

1. Connect to the open SAP GUI session


2. Navigate to the Users by complex selection criteria screen


3. Open the Role Assignment table


4. Right-click the table


5. Choose Spreadsheet


6. Save the file automatically as .xlsx



Below is a basic VBA macro template you can modify.


---

1. Requirements

Before using the macro:

1. SAP GUI Scripting must be enabled

In SAP:
Alt + F12 → Options → Accessibility & Scripting → Enable scripting



2. Excel VBA enabled


3. SAP session already open




---

2. VBA Macro Example

Open Excel → VBA Editor (ALT + F11) → Module → Paste this code

Sub ExportSAPRoleAssignment()

    Dim SapGuiAuto As Object
    Dim SAPApp As Object
    Dim SAPCon As Object
    Dim session As Object
    
    Dim SavePath As String
    
    'File save location
    SavePath = "C:\SAPExports\RoleAssignment.xlsx"

    'Connect to SAP
    Set SapGuiAuto = GetObject("SAPGUI")
    Set SAPApp = SapGuiAuto.GetScriptingEngine
    Set SAPCon = SAPApp.Children(0)
    Set session = SAPCon.Children(0)

    'Make sure SAP window is active
    session.findById("wnd[0]").maximize
    
    'Right click the Role Assignment table
    session.findById("wnd[0]/usr/cntlGRID1/shellcont/shell").contextMenu
    
    'Select Spreadsheet export
    session.findById("wnd[0]/usr/cntlGRID1/shellcont/shell").selectContextMenuItem "&XXL"
    
    'Choose XLSX format
    session.findById("wnd[1]/usr/radRB_OTHERS").Select
    
    'Continue
    session.findById("wnd[1]/tbar[0]/btn[0]").press
    
    'Save file path
    session.findById("wnd[1]/usr/ctxtDY_PATH").Text = "C:\SAPExports"
    session.findById("wnd[1]/usr/ctxtDY_FILENAME").Text = "RoleAssignment.xlsx"
    
    'Save
    session.findById("wnd[1]/tbar[0]/btn[11]").press

    MsgBox "Export completed!"

End Sub


---

3. How to Get the Correct SAP Object IDs (Important)

Every SAP system has different control IDs like:

wnd[0]/usr/cntlGRID1/shellcont/shell

To get the exact IDs:

1. Open SAP


2. Press Alt + F12


3. Click Script Recording and Playback


4. Click Record


5. Perform:

Right click Role Assignment table

Spreadsheet

Save



6. Stop recording



SAP will generate a .vbs script.
You can copy the relevant lines into your Excel VBA.


---

4. Typical SAP Recorded Line for Spreadsheet Export

Usually it looks like this:

session.findById("wnd[0]/usr/cntlGRID1/shellcont/shell").pressToolbarContextButton "&MB_EXPORT"
session.findById("wnd[0]/usr/cntlGRID1/shellcont/shell").selectContextMenuItem "&XXL"

&XXL = Spreadsheet export.


---

5. Recommended Improvement

Instead of overwriting the file, generate a timestamped filename:

SavePath = "C:\SAPExports\RoleAssignment_" & Format(Now, "yyyymmdd_hhmmss") & ".xlsx"


